msgid "1. You start with «%s», 5 peasants and room for 5 people only."
msgstr "1. You start with «%s», 5 peasants and room for 5 people only."

msgid "10 August."
msgstr "10 August."

msgid "19 September. The king's tent. The lords are tired, many of them with yellowed faces."
msgstr "19 September. The king's tent. The lords are tired, many of them with yellowed faces."

msgid "2. Send peasants to the forest, then build «%s»: +5 population."
msgstr "2. Send peasants to the forest, then build «%s»: +5 population."

msgid "25 July. After Grunwald everyone thought the Order was finished. Pan Jan said his great-grandfather thought so too, until he saw Malbork. Plauen burned his own town the day before we came, so that we would have nowhere to pitch a tent."
msgstr "25 July. After Grunwald everyone thought the Order was finished. Pan Jan said his great-grandfather thought so too, until he saw Malbork. Plauen burned his own town the day before we came, so that we would have nowhere to pitch a tent."

msgid "26 July, evening. Ladders are set against the town wall. A knight with the Grzymała arms is the first to get over the battlements."
msgstr "26 July, evening. Ladders are set against the town wall. A knight with the Grzymała arms is the first to get over the battlements."

msgid "3. Build «%s» by the forest and put a peasant on it."
msgstr "3. Build «%s» by the forest and put a peasant on it."

msgid "4. Click «%s» and train more peasants (50 food each)."
msgstr "4. Click «%s» and train more peasants (50 food each)."

msgid "5. Build «%s», «%s» or «%s» and train an army."
msgstr "5. Build «%s», «%s» or «%s» and train an army."

msgid "A Samogitian's hand does not shake, Lord Jakub. The heart shakes, and in battle it is not needed."
msgstr "A Samogitian's hand does not shake, Lord Jakub. The heart shakes, and in battle it is not needed."

msgid "A barrier of felled trees laid in the forest. Nobody passes it; fire burns it away."
msgstr "A barrier of felled trees laid in the forest. Nobody passes it; fire burns it away."

msgid "A battery of wicker gabions. Bombards fire only from here: they stand by it and dig in, two at most."
msgstr "A battery of wicker gabions. Bombards fire only from here: they stand by it and dig in, two at most."

msgid "A brother priest: consecrates the land and casts the Order's spells."
msgstr "A brother priest: consecrates the land and casts the Order's spells."

msgid "A burned wall has fallen. The ones still standing fall the same way: keep the batteries' guard away from them."
msgstr "A burned wall has fallen. The ones still standing fall the same way: keep the batteries' guard away from them."

msgid "A castle, the stronghold of the land: trains the best troops and houses many people. Like a town centre, it keeps your side in the game."
msgstr "A castle, the stronghold of the land: trains the best troops and houses many people. Like a town centre, it keeps your side in the game."

msgid "A chapel by the road. The prince gets down from his horse and goes inside for a moment. A lamp burns before the icon."
msgstr "A chapel by the road. The prince gets down from his horse and goes inside for a moment. A lamp burns before the icon."

msgid "A chapel of the Order. It gathers Power for spells and consecrates the land: shrines of other sides near it give half the Power."
msgstr "A chapel of the Order. It gathers Power for spells and consecrates the land: shrines of other sides near it give half the Power."

msgid "A church: trains priests and researches the faith's improvements."
msgstr "A church: trains priests and researches the faith's improvements."

msgid "A crash. A span of the bridge fell into the water, and the men on it with it."
msgstr "A crash. A span of the bridge fell into the water, and the men on it with it."

msgid "A crossbowman: slow to load, hits hard."
msgstr "A crossbowman: slow to load, hits hard."

msgid "A fast light horseman with javelins."
msgstr "A fast light horseman with javelins."

msgid "A field. A peasant working it brings in food; when it is worked out, it is sown again for its price."
msgstr "A field. A peasant working it brings in food; when it is worked out, it is sown again for its price."

msgid "A foot servant who follows the knight's lance and steadies the ranks."
msgstr "A foot servant who follows the knight's lance and steadies the ranks."

msgid "A gate in your wall: your own people pass, enemies have to break it down. One or two archers on it shoot at enemies nearby."
msgstr "A gate in your wall: your own people pass, enemies have to break it down. One or two archers on it shoot at enemies nearby."

msgid "A guest knight has given himself up. His ransom will be paid in silver."
msgstr "A guest knight has given himself up. His ransom will be paid in silver."

msgid "A half-brother in a grey cloak: the Order's medium horse."
msgstr "A half-brother in a grey cloak: the Order's medium horse."

msgid "A heavy Lithuanian lancer."
msgstr "A heavy Lithuanian lancer."

msgid "A heavy bombard that breaks walls, firing only from a battery."
msgstr "A heavy bombard that breaks walls, firing only from a battery."

msgid "A hidden place of power gives one charge of Power. Stand the prince on it and cast «Wolf Trail»: a trail opens from it through the old forest or the bog for a minute, and on it the dogs find no scent."
msgstr "A hidden place of power gives one charge of Power. Stand the prince on it and cast «Wolf Trail»: a trail opens from it through the old forest or the bog for a minute, and on it the dogs find no scent."

msgid "A hive hollowed out in a forest tree. Two peasants take honey from it: food that never runs out."
msgstr "A hive hollowed out in a forest tree. Two peasants take honey from it: food that never runs out."

msgid "A house feeds more mouths. Train peasants at the yard and build a granary near the food."
msgstr "A house feeds more mouths. Train peasants at the yard and build a granary near the food."

msgid "A knight brother in a white cloak: the Order's heavy horse."
msgstr "A knight brother in a white cloak: the Order's heavy horse."

msgid "A knight's lance strikes hardest at a gallop over open ground. After the blow pull it back and charge again: in a long melee the lance loses its edge."
msgstr "A knight's lance strikes hardest at a gallop over open ground. After the blow pull it back and charge again: in a long melee the lance loses its edge."

msgid "A knight's lance: the Crown's heavy horse, terrible in the charge."
msgstr "A knight's lance: the Crown's heavy horse, terrible in the charge."

msgid "A light horseman from the Prussian lands."
msgstr "A light horseman from the Prussian lands."

msgid "A new age opens new buildings, troops and improvements."
msgstr "A new age opens new buildings, troops and improvements."

msgid "A pavisier: sets up a big shield to cover the shooters behind him."
msgstr "A pavisier: sets up a big shield to cover the shooters behind him."

msgid "A priest must stand by the cross."
msgstr "A priest must stand by the cross."

msgid "A priest: sets up the wayside cross and the chapel, heals those around him and casts the Crown's spells."
msgstr "A priest: sets up the wayside cross and the chapel, heals those around him and casts the Crown's spells."

msgid "A shipman who stays by a bombard for 8 seconds spikes it, and it fires no more. A smith mends a spiked bombard: build a field forge and bring the gun to it."
msgstr "A shipman who stays by a bombard for 8 seconds spikes it, and it fires no more. A smith mends a spiked bombard: build a field forge and bring the gun to it."

msgid "A shot. The ball strikes the wall above the window and sticks there."
msgstr "A shot. The ball strikes the wall above the window and sticks there."

msgid "A shrine stands on it"
msgstr "A shrine stands on it"

msgid "A silver mine (grey blocks on a hill) gives silver."
msgstr "A silver mine (grey blocks on a hill) gives silver."

msgid "A smithy: researches better weapons and armor for your troops."
msgstr "A smithy: researches better weapons and armor for your troops."

msgid "A sortie from Dubysa! Beat it back and take the post again: while a post is lost, the blockade does not work."
msgstr "A sortie from Dubysa! Beat it back and take the post again: while a post is lost, the blockade does not work."

msgid "A store at the forest edge: woodcutters carry wood a shorter way. Researches forestry improvements."
msgstr "A store at the forest edge: woodcutters carry wood a shorter way. Researches forestry improvements."

msgid "A store by bog ore or a silver mine: miners carry a shorter way. Researches mining improvements."
msgstr "A store by bog ore or a silver mine: miners carry a shorter way. Researches mining improvements."

msgid "A store for food near the fields: peasants carry the harvest a shorter way. Researches farming improvements."
msgstr "A store for food near the fields: peasants carry the harvest a shorter way. Researches farming improvements."

msgid "A sturdy archer of the castle garrisons."
msgstr "A sturdy archer of the castle garrisons."

msgid "A tabor takes 3 wagons; inside it +1 melee and +1 pierce armor more."
msgstr "A tabor takes 3 wagons; inside it +1 melee and +1 pierce armor more."

msgid "A tower with three or four archers shooting at enemies in range. Palisades and walls join onto it."
msgstr "A tower with three or four archers shooting at enemies in range. Palisades and walls join onto it."

msgid "A town that swears will feed us. A town that does not get here will feed Plauen."
msgstr "A town that swears will feed us. A town that does not get here will feed Plauen."

msgid "A trading house. Trade is not in this version yet."
msgstr "A trading house. Trade is not in this version yet."

msgid "A wagon of the baggage train."
msgstr "A wagon of the baggage train."

msgid "A wagon of the baggage train; four of them make a tabor."
msgstr "A wagon of the baggage train; four of them make a tabor."

msgid "A wall of sharpened stakes: drag to lay a line. Holds enemies off until they break through; it burns."
msgstr "A wall of sharpened stakes: drag to lay a line. Holds enemies off until they break through; it burns."

msgid "A watchtower of the border watch: it sees all round, by day further still."
msgstr "A watchtower of the border watch: it sees all round, by day further still."

msgid "A wayside cross on a place of power. It gathers Power for spells; with a priest by it the cross can be made a chapel that gives twice as much."
msgstr "A wayside cross on a place of power. It gathers Power for spells; with a priest by it the cross can be made a chapel that gives twice as much."

msgid "A wise woman: heals those around her and casts the Duchy's spells."
msgstr "A wise woman: heals those around her and casts the Duchy's spells."

msgid "A wooden church. In the campaign the peasants who work near it are baptized; its priests and improvements are not in the game yet."
msgstr "A wooden church. In the campaign the peasants who work near it are baptized; its priests and improvements are not in the game yet."

msgid "Abilities"
msgstr "Abilities"

msgid "About noon Prince Bulgakov-Golitsa, without waiting for Chelyadnin, struck our left flank, where the royal court banners stood."
msgstr "About noon Prince Bulgakov-Golitsa, without waiting for Chelyadnin, struck our left flank, where the royal court banners stood."

msgid "About the game"
msgstr "About the game"

msgid "Advance to the next age"
msgstr "Advance to the next age"

msgid "Advance to: %s"
msgstr "Advance to: %s"

msgid "After %d s of melee without a new charge: −%d damage"
msgstr "After %d s of melee without a new charge: −%d damage"

msgid "After the death of Vytautas the Grand Duchy split in two. Sigismund Kęstutaitis holds Vilnius, Trakai and Samogitia; Polotsk, Vitebsk and Smolensk went over to Švitrigaila, and the Livonian knights ride with him. Now Švitrigaila marches on Vilnius, and Sigismund has sent his son Michael against him, with the Poles of Jakub of Kobylany. Mikołaj Gintovt leads his banner in Michael's army. His brother Jurij rides with Švitrigaila."
msgstr "After the death of Vytautas the Grand Duchy split in two. Sigismund Kęstutaitis holds Vilnius, Trakai and Samogitia; Polotsk, Vitebsk and Smolensk went over to Švitrigaila, and the Livonian knights ride with him. Now Švitrigaila marches on Vilnius, and Sigismund has sent his son Michael against him, with the Poles of Jakub of Kobylany. Mikołaj Gintovt leads his banner in Michael's army. His brother Jurij rides with Švitrigaila."

msgid "After the death of great Vytautas the Grand Duchy became like one coat for two. Vilnius pulls one way, Polotsk the other, and the seams crack."
msgstr "After the death of great Vytautas the Grand Duchy became like one coat for two. Vilnius pulls one way, Polotsk the other, and the seams crack."

msgid "Afterwards they told that a mist stood over the ravine and hid our guns. I was there. It was the usual morning haze in the bushes, and a ravine deeper than it looks from the saddle. And yet Andrei stood by the oak longer than I did."
msgstr "Afterwards they told that a mist stood over the ravine and hid our guns. I was there. It was the usual morning haze in the bushes, and a ravine deeper than it looks from the saddle. And yet Andrei stood by the oak longer than I did."

msgid "Age"
msgstr "Age"

msgid "Ages"
msgstr "Ages"

msgid "Aggressive"
msgstr "Aggressive"

msgid "All places of power held for five minutes."
msgstr "All places of power held for five minutes."

msgid "All three Smolensk banners fall"
msgstr "All three Smolensk banners fall"

msgid "All three Smolensk banners have fallen. The wings are torn apart."
msgstr "All three Smolensk banners have fallen. The wings are torn apart."

msgid "Always on"
msgstr "Always on"

msgid "An alka, a pagan sanctuary. It gathers Power for spells and trains wise women; near it their spells recharge faster."
msgstr "An alka, a pagan sanctuary. It gathers Power for spells and trains wise women; near it their spells recharge faster."

msgid "An archer at home in the forest."
msgstr "An archer at home in the forest."

msgid "An oak can be cut down. But the place where it grew is still here. Set stones in a circle, as your grandfather did, and the fire will come back."
msgstr "An oak can be cut down. But the place where it grew is still here. Set stones in a circle, as your grandfather did, and the fire will come back."

msgid "An old oak above the stream. Grandfather spoke of such trees."
msgstr "An old oak above the stream. Grandfather spoke of such trees."

msgid "And about the grove?"
msgstr "And about the grove?"

msgid "And my grandfather Jurij asked all his life that his brother be told he bore him no grudge."
msgstr "And my grandfather Jurij asked all his life that his brother be told he bore him no grudge."

msgid "And the next year the churches in Samogitia burned again. Great-grandfather took no part in it. But he gave away none of the people who burned them."
msgstr "And the next year the churches in Samogitia burned again. Great-grandfather took no part in it. But he gave away none of the people who burned them."

msgid "And the straw broke, as Lord Jakub had said. The ones in front did not know what was with the ones behind, and the ones behind thought the ones in front were already being beaten."
msgstr "And the straw broke, as Lord Jakub had said. The ones in front did not know what was with the ones behind, and the ones behind thought the ones in front were already being beaten."

msgid "And what if they are watching from the far bank?"
msgstr "And what if they are watching from the far bank?"

msgid "And who saw it, apart from you?"
msgstr "And who saw it, apart from you?"

msgid "And whose man are you?"
msgstr "And whose man are you?"

msgid "And will it?"
msgstr "And will it?"

msgid "And you?"
msgstr "And you?"

msgid "Andrei Gintovt falls"
msgstr "Andrei Gintovt falls"

msgid "Andrei Gintovt falls or is left on the far bank"
msgstr "Andrei Gintovt falls or is left on the far bank"

msgid "Andrei Gintovt has fallen. His banner has nobody to carry it home."
msgstr "Andrei Gintovt has fallen. His banner has nobody to carry it home."

msgid "Andrei Gintovt has fallen. Slutsk is left without his men."
msgstr "Andrei Gintovt has fallen. Slutsk is left without his men."

msgid "Andrei Gintovt has fallen. The chronicler wrote his name in the list of the dead."
msgstr "Andrei Gintovt has fallen. The chronicler wrote his name in the list of the dead."

msgid "Andrei Gintovt stayed on the far bank and was taken captive along with the hetman."
msgstr "Andrei Gintovt stayed on the far bank and was taken captive along with the hetman."

msgid "Andrei Gintovt, Princess Anastasia or Prince Yuri falls"
msgstr "Andrei Gintovt, Princess Anastasia or Prince Yuri falls"

msgid "Andrei stood by that oak longer than he needed to. The znakharka who rode with his men said afterwards that the oak gave her one mist, and no more."
msgstr "Andrei stood by that oak longer than he needed to. The znakharka who rode with his men said afterwards that the oak gave her one mist, and no more."

msgid "Andrei takes off the old woven belt with the Samogitian pattern, his great-grandfather's, the one grandfather Jurij carried away east, and ties it on the lowest branch of the oak. Then he goes to his own and does not look back."
msgstr "Andrei takes off the old woven belt with the Samogitian pattern, his great-grandfather's, the one grandfather Jurij carried away east, and ties it on the lowest branch of the oak. Then he goes to his own and does not look back."

msgid "Andrei turns at a call. When he looks at the oak again, there is nobody under it."
msgstr "Andrei turns at a call. When he looks at the oak again, there is nobody under it."

msgid "Andrei's men are thrown back into the Dnieper."
msgstr "Andrei's men are thrown back into the Dnieper."

msgid "Another lord"
msgstr "Another lord"

msgid "Archbishop Jan"
msgstr "Archbishop Jan"

msgid "Archers among the trees are harder to hit. Let the spearmen hold the Order's men while your archers shoot from the forest."
msgstr "Archers among the trees are harder to hit. Let the spearmen hold the Order's men while your archers shoot from the forest."

msgid "Archers: +1 pierce damage and +1 range."
msgstr "Archers: +1 pierce damage and +1 range."

msgid "Are you the Gintaut who burned the chapel?"
msgstr "Are you the Gintaut who burned the chapel?"

msgid "Armor %d melee / %d pierce"
msgstr "Armor %d melee / %d pierce"

msgid "Army"
msgstr "Army"

msgid "As many as came back from the Vedrosha."
msgstr "As many as came back from the Vedrosha."

msgid "As many as there are. We will count in the morning."
msgstr "As many as there are. We will count in the morning."

msgid "At dawn cross the stream by the middle ford and stand on the road in the column's middle. The znakharka's «Bog mist» can hide the crossing."
msgstr "At dawn cross the stream by the middle ford and stand on the road in the column's middle. The znakharka's «Bog mist» can hide the crossing."

msgid "At dawn on the first of September they went. In front the Germans in white cloaks, behind them the princes, at the back the wagons and the Tatars. A long column, and all of it side-on to us."
msgstr "At dawn on the first of September they went. In front the Germans in white cloaks, behind them the princes, at the back the wagons and the Tatars. A long column, and all of it side-on to us."

msgid "At dawn the guns are still on the far bank"
msgstr "At dawn the guns are still on the far bank"

msgid "At most %d at a time"
msgstr "At most %d at a time"

msgid "At most %d for each castle"
msgstr "At most %d for each castle"

msgid "At the end of July Smolensk opened its gates to Vasily III. Hetman Prince Konstanty Ostrogski, seven years out of Muscovite captivity, has gathered the army of the Duchy and the Polish horse and foot of King Sigismund. The Muscovites under the boyar Ivan Chelyadnin stand beyond the Dnieper and guard the bridges at Orsha. The hetman will cross elsewhere, by night. Andrei Gintovt once found him a ford; tonight he must find another one. In the hetman's tent there is a scribe with an inkwell at his belt, and he too is a Gintovt."
msgstr "At the end of July Smolensk opened its gates to Vasily III. Hetman Prince Konstanty Ostrogski, seven years out of Muscovite captivity, has gathered the army of the Duchy and the Polish horse and foot of King Sigismund. The Muscovites under the boyar Ivan Chelyadnin stand beyond the Dnieper and guard the bridges at Orsha. The hetman will cross elsewhere, by night. Andrei Gintovt once found him a ford; tonight he must find another one. In the hetman's tent there is a scribe with an inkwell at his belt, and he too is a Gintovt."

msgid "At the end of September Prince Konstanty was in Vilnius, and at the end of November King Sigismund made him hetman again. Of the oath given in Moscow he never once spoke in our hearing."
msgstr "At the end of September Prince Konstanty was in Vilnius, and at the end of November King Sigismund made him hetman again. Of the oath given in Moscow he never once spoke in our hearing."

msgid "Attack any enemy they see and chase it."
msgstr "Attack any enemy they see and chase it."

msgid "Axemen ride for the bridge with axes and fire. Drive them off to win time: the bridge cannot be saved, but every minute brings more men over it."
msgstr "Axemen ride for the bridge with axes and fire. Drive them off to win time: the bridge cannot be saved, but every minute brings more men over it."

msgid "B next, F turn, Shift keep placing, Esc or right click cancel"
msgstr "B next, F turn, Shift keep placing, Esc or right click cancel"

msgid "Back"
msgstr "Back"

msgid "Back to the game (F2)"
msgstr "Back to the game (F2)"

msgid "Banners taken captive: %d"
msgstr "Banners taken captive: %d"

msgid "Baptize 10 peasants at the church"
msgstr "Baptize 10 peasants at the church"

msgid "Baptized: %d"
msgstr "Baptized: %d"

msgid "Beat back the first assault"
msgstr "Beat back the first assault"

msgid "Beat back the night assault and the fire"
msgstr "Beat back the night assault and the fire"

msgid "Beat back the raid across the border ford"
msgstr "Beat back the raid across the border ford"

msgid "Beat the forward regiment and take the bridge"
msgstr "Beat the forward regiment and take the bridge"

msgid "Beaten men surrounded from two sides lay down their arms. Captive princes count for the extra objective."
msgstr "Beaten men surrounded from two sides lay down their arms. Captive princes count for the extra objective."

msgid "Begin"
msgstr "Begin"

msgid "Begin the battle"
msgstr "Begin the battle"

msgid "Being taken apart"
msgstr "Being taken apart"

msgid "Being taken apart: %d%%"
msgstr "Being taken apart: %d%%"

msgid "Better my hands than someone else's."
msgstr "Better my hands than someone else's."

msgid "Bishop Piotr"
msgstr "Bishop Piotr"

msgid "Bog ore"
msgstr "Bog ore"

msgid "Bog ore (brown blocks in the bog) gives iron."
msgstr "Bog ore (brown blocks in the bog) gives iron."

msgid "Bogurodzica costs 30% less Power."
msgstr "Bogurodzica costs 30% less Power."

msgid "Bogurodzica, dziewica..."
msgstr "Bogurodzica, dziewica..."

msgid "Bombards brought to Sztum: %d"
msgstr "Bombards brought to Sztum: %d"

msgid "Bombards cross the canal and the streams only by the roads. The garrison will come out after you: cover the tail of the column."
msgstr "Bombards cross the canal and the streams only by the roads. The garrison will come out after you: cover the tail of the column."

msgid "Bombards spiked: %d"
msgstr "Bombards spiked: %d"

msgid "Both bridges stand. The foot and the guns are going over them."
msgstr "Both bridges stand. The foot and the guns are going over them."

msgid "Boyar"
msgstr "Boyar"

msgid "Boyar lances strike hard in a charge. To set wood on fire, select units and Alt+right-click an enemy building: they will carry torches to it."
msgstr "Boyar lances strike hard in a charge. To set wood on fire, select units and Alt+right-click an enemy building: they will carry torches to it."

msgid "Bread first. Then the Germans."
msgstr "Bread first. Then the Germans."

msgid "Break the Livonian banners of Nesselrode and Kerskorf"
msgstr "Break the Livonian banners of Nesselrode and Kerskorf"

msgid "Breaks other sides' spells; a creature loses 150 HP and falls back."
msgstr "Breaks other sides' spells; a creature loses 150 HP and falls back."

msgid "Brickworks: while one stands, your towers, walls and castles cost less."
msgstr "Brickworks: while one stands, your towers, walls and castles cost less."

msgid "Bridge %d: %d of %d sections"
msgstr "Bridge %d: %d of %d sections"

msgid "Bridge: %d%%"
msgstr "Bridge: %d%%"

msgid "Bring Jaśko to the fallen banner within 60 seconds. While it is down, the whole Polish army has lost the spirit it gave."
msgstr "Bring Jaśko to the fallen banner within 60 seconds. While it is down, the whole Polish army has lost the spirit it gave."

msgid "Bring Yuri back from the sortie alive and unhurt"
msgstr "Bring Yuri back from the sortie alive and unhurt"

msgid "Bring all three servants through"
msgstr "Bring all three servants through"

msgid "Bring back at least 15 units"
msgstr "Bring back at least 15 units"

msgid "Bring out the banner that lost its standard-bearer"
msgstr "Bring out the banner that lost its standard-bearer"

msgid "Bring the towns' envoys to the king's tent"
msgstr "Bring the towns' envoys to the king's tent"

msgid "Bring your men and the banner back over the river"
msgstr "Bring your men and the banner back over the river"

msgid "Brother Konrad"
msgstr "Brother Konrad"

msgid "Brother priests: +50% HP; Exorcism reaches 2 cells farther."
msgstr "Brother priests: +50% HP; Exorcism reaches 2 cells farther."

msgid "Brother, there is the bloody flux in my camp. I will not lead my men to die of the flux under walls that cannot be taken."
msgstr "Brother, there is the bloody flux in my camp. I will not lead my men to die of the flux under walls that cannot be taken."

msgid "Brought back over the river: %d"
msgstr "Brought back over the river: %d"

msgid "Build a church and baptize your people, send a delegation to the council, beat back the Order's raid and lead the council's envoys through Samogitia. Do not let the Order's evidence reach 100."
msgstr "Build a church and baptize your people, send a delegation to the council, beat back the Order's raid and lead the council's envoys through Samogitia. Do not let the Order's evidence reach 100."

msgid "Build a church in the village by the ford"
msgstr "Build a church in the village by the ford"

msgid "Build a church in the village on the Medininkai road"
msgstr "Build a church in the village on the Medininkai road"

msgid "Build a church in the village south of the yard"
msgstr "Build a church in the village south of the yard"

msgid "Build a wooden church"
msgstr "Build a wooden church"

msgid "Build chapels on both places of power"
msgstr "Build chapels on both places of power"

msgid "Build the church near the yard. Peasants who work near it are baptized one by one."
msgstr "Build the church near the yard. Peasants who work near it are baptized one by one."

msgid "Build «%s» on a place of power: it gives Power for spells."
msgstr "Build «%s» on a place of power: it gives Power for spells."

msgid "Build «%s», «%s» or «%s» and train an army. The Order will come."
msgstr "Build «%s», «%s» or «%s» and train an army. The Order will come."

msgid "Building and training"
