msgstr "Houses %d"

msgid "Hover a button to see its price and why it is not available."
msgstr "Hover a button to see its price and why it is not available."

msgid "How do you know?"
msgstr "How do you know?"

msgid "How many of us are there?"
msgstr "How many of us are there?"

msgid "How many of you?"
msgstr "How many of you?"

msgid "How to play"
msgstr "How to play"

msgid "How to play (F1)"
msgstr "How to play (F1)"

msgid "Hunters' marks. Hunters go where there is no watch. We follow them."
msgstr "Hunters' marks. Hunters go where there is no watch. We follow them."

msgid "I am asking what you think."
msgstr "I am asking what you think."

msgid "I am of the Ruthenian faith too. And how long has Prince Michael been of it?"
msgstr "I am of the Ruthenian faith too. And how long has Prince Michael been of it?"

msgid "I did not make that up, Długosz writes so."
msgstr "I did not make that up, Długosz writes so."

msgid "I kissed the cross in captivity, and I break it myself. Nobody released me and nobody will excuse me. Ask it of me alone."
msgstr "I kissed the cross in captivity, and I break it myself. Nobody released me and nobody will excuse me. Ask it of me alone."

msgid "I know. So ride not to Vitebsk, but further. To the Dnieper, where Sigismund cannot reach."
msgstr "I know. So ride not to Vitebsk, but further. To the Dnieper, where Sigismund cannot reach."

msgid "I see. Drive that banner off, don't cut it down. Whoever touches Lord Jurij will answer to me."
msgstr "I see. Drive that banner off, don't cut it down. Whoever touches Lord Jurij will answer to me."

msgid "I swear to the one the whole land of Vitebsk swears to. As you swear to the one Samogitia swears to. Our faith is one, Mikołaj. Our land is not."
msgstr "I swear to the one the whole land of Vitebsk swears to. As you swear to the one Samogitia swears to. Our faith is one, Mikołaj. Our land is not."

msgid "I think the land does not want them."
msgstr "I think the land does not want them."

msgid "I was at Orsha and heard the guns roar. What I write below I heard from my grandfather, and he from his father. What is true here and what is a tale, judge for yourselves."
msgstr "I was at Orsha and heard the guns roar. What I write below I heard from my grandfather, and he from his father. What is true here and what is a tale, judge for yourselves."

msgid "I was baptized so that the grove would stand. And so that the Germans would go."
msgstr "I was baptized so that the grove would stand. And so that the Germans would go."

msgid "If not us, the Germans will come and baptize us with the sword. Better the Poles, and with water."
msgstr "If not us, the Germans will come and baptize us with the sword. Better the Poles, and with water."

msgid "In August Master Ulrich declared war on King Jogaila and marched on Dobrzyń. In autumn they made a truce until Midsummer Day. All winter both sides forged spears. And our great-grandfather rode beyond the Neman for the first time in his life."
msgstr "In August Master Ulrich declared war on King Jogaila and marched on Dobrzyń. In autumn they made a truce until Midsummer Day. All winter both sides forged spears. And our great-grandfather rode beyond the Neman for the first time in his life."

msgid "In December Plauen wrote that had we stood another fifteen days, his garrison would have died of hunger. Fifteen days. For forty-seven years afterwards the Crown paid for those fifteen days, in blood and in silver. And Jaśko, pan Jan said, could never eat boiled wheat until old age, though it was eaten in the castle and not by us."
msgstr "In December Plauen wrote that had we stood another fifteen days, his garrison would have died of hunger. Fifteen days. For forty-seven years afterwards the Crown paid for those fifteen days, in blood and in silver. And Jaśko, pan Jan said, could never eat boiled wheat until old age, though it was eaten in the castle and not by us."

msgid "In February 1508 the men of Prince Michael Glinski killed his enemy, Marshal Jan Zabrzeziński, near Grodno, and Glinski went over to Vasily III. With two or three thousand horse and Muscovite detachments he marched on the towns of the Duchy. Slutsk is ruled by the widowed Princess Anastasia for her son Yuri, sixteen years old. The rebels have no guns that can break a wall: only ladders, fire and cavalry. Andrei Gintovt has come with the men who came back from the Vedrosha."
msgstr "In February 1508 the men of Prince Michael Glinski killed his enemy, Marshal Jan Zabrzeziński, near Grodno, and Glinski went over to Vasily III. With two or three thousand horse and Muscovite detachments he marched on the towns of the Duchy. Slutsk is ruled by the widowed Princess Anastasia for her son Yuri, sixteen years old. The rebels have no guns that can break a wall: only ladders, fire and cavalry. Andrei Gintovt has come with the men who came back from the Vedrosha."

msgid "In Konstanz the fathers of the council had gathered to judge three popes at once. Our people were to go there too and tell how the Order baptized Samogitia."
msgstr "In Konstanz the fathers of the council had gathered to judge three popes at once. Our people were to go there too and tell how the Order baptized Samogitia."

msgid "In October fourteen hundred and seventeen Samogitia got its own bishop, Matthias of Trakai. He spoke our tongue. Now the Order had nothing to tell the council: the Samogitians were baptized, and it was not the Order that baptized them."
msgstr "In October fourteen hundred and seventeen Samogitia got its own bishop, Matthias of Trakai. He spoke our tongue. Now the Order had nothing to tell the council: the Samogitians were baptized, and it was not the Order that baptized them."

msgid "In Slutsk they still tell of a passage under the castle hill. I have not seen it. But Andrei saw it, and said it was narrow there and smelled of the river."
msgstr "In Slutsk they still tell of a passage under the castle hill. I have not seen it. But Andrei saw it, and said it was narrow there and smelled of the river."

msgid "In close order the men around him lose half as much morale"
msgstr "In close order the men around him lose half as much morale"

msgid "In spring they stood on the bog, they drink river water and eat old grain. Think what you like."
msgstr "In spring they stood on the bog, they drink river water and eat old grain. Think what you like."

msgid "In the camp they have found him gone. The centurion Nezhdan's chase will set out for the ford; every new alarm brings it nearer."
msgstr "In the camp they have found him gone. The centurion Nezhdan's chase will set out for the ford; every new alarm brings it nearer."

msgid "In the dusk behind the wagon a red kaftan flickers. Jaśko goes there, but there is only a strange carter in a rust-coloured shirt."
msgstr "In the dusk behind the wagon a red kaftan flickers. Jaśko goes there, but there is only a strange carter in a rust-coloured shirt."

msgid "In the middle is the stream. Gintovt, do your Samogitians know the ford?"
msgstr "In the middle is the stream. Gintovt, do your Samogitians know the ford?"

msgid "In the middle of the Polish line the white eagle sways over the press, leans and is gone. For a moment it is quiet. The Order's knights shout something joyful."
msgstr "In the middle of the Polish line the white eagle sways over the press, leans and is gone. For a moment it is quiet. The Order's knights shout something joyful."

msgid "In the spring of 1500 border princes went over to Ivan III with their lands, and war began. In May the Muscovites of Yuri Koshkin took Dorogobuzh. Hetman Prince Konstanty Ostrogski has come from Smolensk through Yelnya to win it back; Prince Daniil Shchenya has joined the Muscovite army and leads it now. Their camp stands on Mitkovo field beyond the Trosna, and there is one bridge over the Trosna. Andrei Gintovt, of the family's younger branch on the Dnieper, carries his banner for the first time."
msgstr "In the spring of 1500 border princes went over to Ivan III with their lands, and war began. In May the Muscovites of Yuri Koshkin took Dorogobuzh. Hetman Prince Konstanty Ostrogski has come from Smolensk through Yelnya to win it back; Prince Daniil Shchenya has joined the Muscovite army and leads it now. Their camp stands on Mitkovo field beyond the Trosna, and there is one bridge over the Trosna. Andrei Gintovt, of the family's younger branch on the Dnieper, carries his banner for the first time."

msgid "In the year of our Lord fourteen hundred and ten, on the fifteenth of July, our great-grandfather Gintaut stood in the right wing, under the hand of Vytautas. They stood a long time, in the sun, in iron."
msgstr "In the year of our Lord fourteen hundred and ten, on the fifteenth of July, our great-grandfather Gintaut stood in the right wing, under the hand of Vytautas. They stood a long time, in the sun, in iron."

msgid "In two minutes the Order's raid will come across the border ford in the west."
msgstr "In two minutes the Order's raid will come across the border ford in the west."

msgid "In work: %s, %d%%"
msgstr "In work: %s, %d%%"

msgid "Intercept the Order's grain convoy on the river road"
msgstr "Intercept the Order's grain convoy on the river road"

msgid "Iron"
msgstr "Iron"

msgid "Iron is mined faster: +20%."
msgstr "Iron is mined faster: +20%."

msgid "Iron: right-click bog ore (brown blocks in the bog) with peasants."
msgstr "Iron: right-click bog ore (brown blocks in the bog) with peasants."

msgid "Is Samogitia ours now, prince?"
msgstr "Is Samogitia ours now, prince?"

msgid "Is that their oak?"
msgstr "Is that their oak?"

msgid "Is the army set out?"
msgstr "Is the army set out?"

msgid "It has gone out for good"
msgstr "It has gone out for good"

msgid "It is an oak, my lord. Just an old one."
msgstr "It is an oak, my lord. Just an old one."

msgid "It is hot. Lances in the sun tire and lose heart; in the shade of the grove and in the wet hollows they rest. The Order has stood in the sun since morning. Do not hurry."
msgstr "It is hot. Lances in the sun tire and lose heart; in the shade of the grove and in the wet hollows they rest. The Order has stood in the sun since morning. Do not hurry."

msgid "It needs two other first-age buildings and opens new units."
msgstr "It needs two other first-age buildings and opens new units."

msgid "It rained in the night. Their powder is as wet as their prayers. Hold!"
msgstr "It rained in the night. Their powder is as wet as their prayers. Hold!"

msgid "It was your men who came across the ford."
msgstr "It was your men who came across the ford."

msgid "It will be done, prince."
msgstr "It will be done, prince."

msgid "It will be ours. By peace, not by the sword. With the sword we have done all we could."
msgstr "It will be ours. By peace, not by the sword. With the sword we have done all we could."

msgid "Jakub's men are over the wall and will open the gate from inside. Go into the town after them, to St John's church under the castle wall."
msgstr "Jakub's men are over the wall and will open the gate from inside. Go into the town after them, to St John's church under the castle wall."

msgid "Jan. So be it. Only my grandfather called me Gintaut, and the grove knows me by that name."
msgstr "Jan. So be it. Only my grandfather called me Gintaut, and the grove knows me by that name."

msgid "Javelin: %d damage at %d cells, every %d s"
msgstr "Javelin: %d damage at %d cells, every %d s"

msgid "Jaśko by the battery. In one of the windows of the great hall something red flashes. The gunner hastily lays the barrel."
msgstr "Jaśko by the battery. In one of the windows of the great hall something red flashes. The gunner hastily lays the barrel."

msgid "Jaśko falls"
msgstr "Jaśko falls"

msgid "Jaśko falls under the walls of Malbork."
msgstr "Jaśko falls under the walls of Malbork."

msgid "Jaśko has «The Pact». Once in this mission: for 30 seconds the units around him lose no spirit and strike harder. It costs no Power. What it costs, you will learn later."
msgstr "Jaśko has «The Pact». Once in this mission: for 30 seconds the units around him lose no spirit and strike harder. It costs no Power. What it costs, you will learn later."

msgid "Jaśko is struck from his horse and carried off the field."
msgstr "Jaśko is struck from his horse and carried off the field."

msgid "Jaśko's banners are cut to pieces"
msgstr "Jaśko's banners are cut to pieces"

msgid "Jaśko's banners have been cut to pieces."
msgstr "Jaśko's banners have been cut to pieces."

msgid "Jurij Gintovt's banner can be put to flight but not destroyed."
msgstr "Jurij Gintovt's banner can be put to flight but not destroyed."

msgid "Jurij took the woven belt off the staff and threw it across the stream. It fell into the water at the feet of Mikołaj's horse."
msgstr "Jurij took the woven belt off the staff and threw it across the stream. It fell into the water at the feet of Mikołaj's horse."

